geeklist.comment:
[q="shaneben"][q="CaliSeddon"]I volunteer for a charity A Heart to Give here in Orlando, and they always need gifts for Tweens/Teens/Families for Birthdays and Christmas. If you've a NEW and SEALED game that is easy for non-gamers to play (Think something you would find at Target or Walmart), I'll probably buy it from you for $5. Sorry I can't do more, $5 adds up fast!  LMK[/q]

@Cali will you take opened games as a donation for your charity? I have several games that if they don't sell I would much rather them go to a charity. The games would fit the family game category as well. [/q]
I would love to take them, but A Heart To Give has rules about donations, and they have to be New and Sealed toys to ensure there are no missing pieces or that something isn't broken. Plus I think the idea is that every child deserves something new and shiny all their own. Thank you for your offer though!
